The attached image, Figure 5, demonstrates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the uptake of adsorbed antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs). Panel (A), a flow cytometry dot plot, shows that while soluble ovalbumin (OVA) or Nano-11 alone are minimally taken up by BMDCs, their combination (Nano-11+OVA) leads to a dramatic increase in antigen-positive cells. Panel (B), a histogram for FITC-OVA, further quantifies this, illustrating a substantial shift in fluorescence intensity for cells treated with Nano-11+OVA compared to soluble OVA or Nano-11 alone, indicating enhanced intracellular antigen delivery.